  <releases>
    <release version="0.9.2" date="2026-11-17">
      <description>
        <p>A keyboard's page now shows its layout (ANSI, ISO, JIS or ABNT2, and the key legends) and lets you change it when detection is wrong, and the Apex 3 TKL's Keys tab draws the right keys for it. Also new: clearer status marks (an icon and a word, in colors that no longer look like the accent), a tidier look for every page, and a fix for the "Send a report" prompt that flashed at start-up. CI and release workflows are also safer. The layout read has not been tried on a real Corsair or Razer keyboard yet, and a Logitech keyboard's layout code is only written into test reports, not used, because what it means is not documented.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.9.1" date="2026-11-16">
      <description>
        <p>Logitech PRO 2 and PRO X 2 DEX wireless ids and a safer save (issue #34), plus three devices from device requests, read only for now: the Razer BlackWidow V4 Mini HyperSpeed, mice on the YJX receiver such as the MAMBASNAKE M4, and the Wraith W60. A mouse without lights no longer shows a Lighting tab, and the G-Shift layer of a read-only mouse can be looked at. The W60 has been read on a real keyboard; nobody has tried the other two yet. Also new: a read-only mode with a log of every write, battery notifications, quick actions from the tray and the command line, a guided "Test my device" page, a mouse tester, and installed games for app profiles.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.9.0" date="2026-11-16">
      <description>
        <p>A light theme and accent colors, with System following the desktop (KDE Plasma and GNOME included), and app profiles on KDE Plasma and GNOME. Settings is tidier: the credits are in their own dialog, the supported brands are listed, and where everything is stored is complete. The program is also smaller and wakes up less. Nothing changes in how PeriHub talks to devices.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.8.4" date="2026-11-15">
      <description>
        <p>On Windows a mouse behind a LIGHTSPEED, Bolt or Unifying receiver is found, and a mouse with a tested memory format can be saved to through its receiver, as an experimental feature. Also: the G502 HERO Wireless's lights have the right names.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.8.3" date="2026-11-14">
      <description>
        <p>A LIGHTSPEED receiver whose mouse does not answer, such as a POWERPLAY mat's, is shown with a test report instead of "No device found", and the mouse test report lists the mouse's HID++ features.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.8.2" date="2026-11-13">
      <description>
        <p>Lighting for Razer mice: the brightness of each light on 47 of them, and one colour that is not saved on 27. Nobody has tried it on a Razer mouse yet: it can be changed at your own risk.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.8.1" date="2026-11-13">
      <description>
        <p>The older Logitech G mice whose software Logitech removed: the G500s and G700s are read and their DPI in use can be changed, the G9, G9x, G500 and G700 are read. Nobody has tried them yet, and PeriHub never writes their memory.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.8.0" date="2026-11-12">
      <description>
        <p>23 more mice, among them Glorious, Roccat, Pulsar, Lamzu, Cooler Master, EVGA and the Logitech G600, and keyboards with QMK or Vial firmware. Nobody has tried them yet: their settings can be changed at your own risk. The sidebar lists only the devices that are there, a page helps ask for a new one, and each zone of the mouse lighting can keep its own effect.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.7.0" date="2026-11-11">
      <description>
        <p>129 mice of three more brands, ASUS ROG and TUF, SteelSeries and Razer, recognized from the published documentation of their protocols. Nobody has tried them yet: their settings can be changed at your own risk.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.6.8" date="2026-11-11">
      <description>
        <p>First version as a Flatpak. Inside it, autostart goes through the desktop's Background portal, and the optional udev rules come with the commands to run.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.6.7" date="2026-11-11">
      <description>
        <p>Logitech mice are supported by the format of their memory instead of by model, and the devices on a Bolt or Unifying receiver get a page of their own, with their DPI as a first experimental setting.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.6.6" date="2026-11-10">
      <description>
        <p>The Logi Bolt receiver is recognized, a first step for the MX Master 3S.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.6.5" date="2026-11-09">
      <description>
        <p>The Logitech G502 X Wireless is supported.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
